{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:abc29392291d952d","name":"Drexl's Gang","source":{"id":"source:reference-abc29392291d952d","title":"Drexl's Gang","revision":19425,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:56:55Z","sha256":"bf11cb726dd28fb9e997861d36acaa4ab66a721f624a52476390200acd668ed6","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19425","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Drexl%27s%20Gang&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-abc29392291d952d","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Drexl's Gang is a small band of thugs, scavengers, and criminals that operates out of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Raxus Prime"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Raxus_Prime","referenceId":"reference:9a3dfa77203e9cf1"},". Drexl has managed to set up a rather impressive salvage operation on the junk-covered planet, and he uses his ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rodian"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rodian","referenceId":"reference:26980c5af3a71c5b"}," minions to produce scrap and other goods that can be sold to offworld traders. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Drexl Roosh"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Drexl_Roosh","referenceId":"reference:9f6904eb25fd568a"}," has little regard for the lives of his gang members, and even less for the lives of those who attempt to interfere with his operation.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Drexl's scavengers pick apart any junk found on the planet, looking for valuable hunks of metal or intact mechanical parts. On many occasions, Drexl's Gang has come into conflict with the Core, the massive computer system that coordinates Raxus Prime's automated labor population. Drexl continues to reap the rewards of his boldness while defying the Core's Droid legions at every turn.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Drexl's Gang Un